  "id": "interactional-synchrony",
  "term": "interactional synchrony",
  "definition": "Interactional synchrony is the way two people’s body movements line up in time during social interaction, either on purpose or spontaneously. It is described as an important part of successful human interaction, and lower synchrony can reflect reduced sensitivity or attention to the other person’s movements.",
